---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const schema = {"@context":"https://schema.org","@graph":[{"@type":"Article","headline":"Where to Stay in Zhangjiajie | Hotels Guide (2026)","description":"Where to stay near Zhangjiajie National Park: Wulingyuan town, city center, and guesthouses inside the park. Price ranges, recommendations, and first-hand experience.","datePublished":"2026-07-01","dateModified":"2026-07-31","author":{"@type":"Person","name":"Zhangjiajie Guide Team"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Where to Stay","item":"https://zhangjiajie-national-park.com/hotels/"}]}]};
const areas = [
  {name:"Wulingyuan Town",price:"CNY 150-800",best:"Most visitors",desc:"The most convenient base. Located directly at the park entrance, with hundreds of hotels, restaurants, and convenience stores within walking distance. You can walk to the park gate in 5-15 minutes depending on your hotel. We have stayed here on four separate trips and never regretted choosing Wulingyuan over the city center. The town has everything you need: ATMs (Bank of China, ICBC), pharmacies, a hospital, and a supermarket.",notes:"Best area for first-time visitors. More expensive than the city but saves you 90 minutes of daily commuting."},
  {name:"Zhangjiajie City Center",price:"CNY 80-500",best:"Budget travelers",desc:"About 40 minutes from the park by bus or taxi. Hotels are significantly cheaper — we have seen clean, comfortable rooms for CNY 100/night that would cost CNY 250 in Wulingyuan. The trade-off is time: you lose about 90 minutes per day commuting. The city has better restaurants, more shopping, and the night market near the train station is worth a visit on its own. This area makes sense if you are on a tight budget or spending only 1-2 days at the park.",notes:"Cheaper but adds travel time. Works well if you are combining Zhangjiajie with Tianmen Mountain (which starts from the city)."},
  {name:"Inside the Park",price:"CNY 200-400",best:"Photographers",desc:"A handful of basic guesthouses operate inside the park boundaries, primarily near Huangshi Village and in a few spots along the Golden Whip Stream. We stayed at one near Huangshi Village in November 2025: the room was spartan (hard bed, shared bathroom) but stepping outside at 6:30 AM to mist-filled valleys and zero other people was worth every inconvenience. These guesthouses fill up fast and are not bookable on international platforms — you typically arrange through your Wulingyuan hotel or a local contact.",notes:"Only for the dedicated. Basic facilities. Not suitable for families or anyone expecting hotel amenities. You need to arrange through local contacts."}
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Where to Stay in Zhangjiajie | Hotels Guide (2026)" description="Where to stay near Zhangjiajie National Park: Wulingyuan town, city center, and guesthouses inside the park. Price ranges verified April 2026, recommendations, and first-hand experience." author="Zhangjiajie Guide Team" datePublished="July 2026">
<slot name="head"><script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}></script></slot>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 md:px-6 pb-20 md:pb-28">
  <div class="inline-flex items-center rounded-full border border-forest-200 bg-forest-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-forest-700 mb-6">Hotels</div>
  <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-stone-900 leading-tight">Where to Stay Near Zhangjiajie</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-stone-500 leading-relaxed">Three main areas, three different experiences. Your choice of where to stay will shape your entire visit — here is what we learned from staying in all three. <span class="text-xs text-stone-400">Prices verified April 2026.</span></p>
  <nav class="mt-6 flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-stone-400" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/" class="hover:text-forest-700 transition-colors">Home</a><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg><span class="text-stone-600">Where to Stay</span></nav>

  

  <div class="mt-8 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
    <picture>
      <source srcset="/banner-hotels.webp" type="image/webp" />
      <img
        src="/banner-hotels.jpg"
        alt="Tianmen Mountain scenery near Wulingyuan accommodation"
        class="w-full aspect-[21/9] object-cover"
        width="1200"
        height="514"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </picture>
  </div>
    <div class="mt-12 space-y-8">
    {areas.map(({name,price,best,desc,notes}) => (
      <section class="rounded-2xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-6 md:p-8">
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-4 mb-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-stone-900">{name}</h2>
          <span class="shrink-0 rounded-full bg-forest-50 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold text-forest-700">{price}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-4"><span class="text-xs text-stone-400">Best for:</span><span class="text-xs font-medium text-stone-600">{best}</span></div>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500 leading-relaxed mb-4">{desc}</p>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-forest-100 bg-forest-50/50 p-3 text-sm text-forest-800">{notes}</div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="mt-16">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-6">Booking Tips</h2>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 text-lg mb-2">Book Ahead in Peak Season</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">July, August, and the first week of October (Golden Week) see Wulingyuan hotels fill up completely. Book at least 2-3 weeks ahead. We made the mistake of booking 3 days ahead in July and had to take a subpar room at double the normal rate.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 text-lg mb-2">Use Chinese Booking Platforms</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">Trip.com (formerly Ctrip) has the best English-language coverage. For more options and lower prices, search on Meituan (美团) or Fliggy (飞猪) — though these are Chinese-language only. Hotels listed only on Chinese platforms are often CNY 50-100 cheaper per night than their Trip.com equivalents.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-stone-200 bg-white p-5">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-stone-800 text-lg mb-2">Confirm Foreigner-Friendly Status</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-stone-500">Not all Chinese hotels are licensed to accept foreign guests. Before booking a budget guesthouse (\&lt;CNY 200/night), message the property to confirm they accept foreign passports — especially important for smaller, family-run places in Wulingyuan. Larger hotels (Pullman, Crowne Plaza, international chains) have no issues.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-16 pt-12 border-t border-stone-200 text-center"><a href="/guide" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-forest-500 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white transition-all hover:bg-forest-600 active:scale-[0.98]">Back to Full Guide <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M6 3l5 5-5 5"/></svg></a></div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
